On 2007-07-23, foosh <dfoosh1@gmail.com> wrote:
> I was perusing the Sporkhack changelog, reading about all the nifty
> additions, subtractions, modifications, when I began to wonder: How
> does the aim/direction of Sporkhack compare with that of SLASH'EM?

I can't really speak for the Slash'Em maintainers, but I know that my
impression is that a _lot_ of things have been added to Slash'Em and a
certain amount of power creep has resulted; this is fine and good for,
say, Slash'Em, but I'd still like Spork to have much of the 'feel' of
Nethack... just differently balanced and tweaked.

So what this means is - no lightsabers.  No machine guns.  In general,
no flagrantly sadistic stuff like the grid bug mkII (though that doesn't 
preclude things that are Just Harder from showing up).

People often make the joke that "Slash'Em wants you dead."  I don't
really want that to be Spork at all; I'd just like to make it a Nethack
with some more variety and some more stuff in general.  I may change
abilities of some roles, or change Quest Artifacts around; this is
largely done so that, say, playing a Knight can be an overall different
experience from playing a Samurai.  It is to some degree in NH already,
but this falls down a lot in the mid- to late-game; I'd like to enhance
that degree for all roles, and make it extend through the _whole_ game,
not just until everyone has the standard Ascension Kit ready.

